
=== Logging
	   
The standalone SymmetricDS installation uses https://logback.qos.ch/[Logback] for logging.  The configuration file is `conf/logback.xml`.
The `logback.xml` file has hints as to what logging can be enabled for useful, finer-grained logging.

There is a command line option to turn on preconfigured debugging levels.  When the `--debug` option is used the `conf/logback-debug.xml` is used instead of `logback.xml`.

SymmetricDS proxies all of its logging through http://www.slf4j.org/[SLF4J].  When deploying to an application server or if Logback is not
being leveraged, then the general rules for SLF4J logging apply.


ifdef::pro[]
You can use the logging screen to dynamically adjust the log level in order to help triage issues.  When developing transforms it is useful to turn on *Log Sync Details*.

image::images/manage/logging.png[]
endif::pro[]
